<binaryimage arch="ARM:LE:32:v7:default">
<!--
    GH-881 part B on 32-bit ARM: a call argument the caller also tests is
    dropped.  The ARM sibling of kuna-calleereadarg.xml.

        int fwd(int *p) { int x = *p; if (x > 5) return x; return ext(x); }

    clang -O2 for armv7a loads x into r0, compares it, returns it with a
    conditional `bxgt lr` and tail-calls ext with it in the same register
    (ldr r0,[r0]; cmp r0,#5; bxgt lr; b ext), and kuna printed `ext();`.
    Funcdata::onlyOpUse refuses the r0 trial because the value also feeds the
    compare and the other path's RETURN.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 active input-trial scoring, option calleereadarg
    off|on.  ext reads r0 on entry, so pass 2 keeps the argument.

    Two controls with a tested value left in an argument register:
      neg      tests r0 and calls g, which reads no argument register: g().
      negpush  tests r2 and calls bar, whose clang -Oz prologue pushes the dead
               r2 and r3 to reserve stack (push {r2, r3, r4, lr}).  That reads
               r3, the last argument register, which is what a register-save
               prologue does too, so it is no evidence: bar() in both passes.
      pick     leaves its tested z in r1 and tail-calls show(11).  show is
               gcc -Os: push {r0, r1, r4, lr} reserves stack with the dead r1
               beside its one parameter, which it also reads with mov r4, r0.
               A register stored only by an instruction that stores several is
               no evidence: show(0xb) in both passes.

    Pass 1 (`option calleereadarg off`) reproduces the BUG: ext() in fwd.
    Pass 2 (`option calleereadarg on`, the default) is the FIX: ext(*a0), and
    the controls are unchanged.
-->
